course: dictionary
lesson: 5472
title: Larva: the young wriggler
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A larva is the young form of an insect, or of some other animals like frogs and fish, after it hatches from its egg and before it changes into an adult. «Look closely at a pond and you may see a tiny tube of stones walking along the bottom» is a clue: that walking tube is a caddis fly larva.
explain: Context helps again. «Newly hatched clownfish drift in the open sea as tiny larvae» tells you larvae come out of eggs and are young, not grown up. «Out of a thousand eggs only a few become adult frogs» shows that adults come after the young stages.
explain: Remember the plural: one larva, many larvae. Say «a larva» for one, and «insect larvae» or «mosquito larvae» for more than one.
fact: A larva is the young form of an animal after it hatches from an egg.
fact: «Larva» means the young form of an insect, or of some animals like frogs and fish, before it becomes an adult.
fact: Many larvae look like worms, such as caterpillars and maggots.
fact: Caterpillars are butterfly larvae, and maggots are fly larvae.
fact: In complete metamorphosis the life cycle goes egg, larva, pupa, adult.
exercise: A caterpillar is a butterfly larva. What is a larva? | A fish that lives on a reef | *The young form of an insect after it hatches from its egg | A pupa wrapped in silk | A grown-up insect that can fly
exercise: «Newly hatched clownfish drift in the open sea as tiny larvae.» Which word tells you larvae come out of eggs? | *hatched | drift | tiny | open
exercise: Which of these is a fly larva? | A pupa | A tadpole | *A maggot | A caterpillar
test: «An axolotl hunts by sucking in worms, insect larvae and small fish.» What is the plural of larva? | *larvae | larvas | larva | larvaes
test: «Caddis fly larvae glue sand grains, tiny shells or plant bits together with silk into a case.» Why do caddis fly larvae build a case? | It is a toy to play with | It helps them fly faster | *It protects their soft bodies from fish | It makes them into adults
exam: Which stage comes straight after the egg in the life cycle of a butterfly? | An adult | *A larva | A wing | A pupa
